## Critical operating rules

- **Trades are anchored by the biggest single asset on each side.** Packages
  of small assets do NOT substitute for a stud even if KTC totals match. The
  user has been explicit about this. Don't propose pile-of-fillers counters.
- **KTC is the source of truth** for both player and pick values. The site
  reads `site/data/ktc.js` (generated by `site/data/build_ktc.py`). Pick
  values come from KTC's `position: "RDP"` entries, NOT the legacy
  `strategy.js::pick_values_1qb` table (which is now fallback only).
- **DSTs and Kickers do NOT appear** in dynasty-asset views. IDP positions
  only appear in IDP leagues.
- **Picks ARE counted** in `computeRosterStrength`. They are NOT counted in the
  projected-finish path (`originSlot` → `startingStrength` with `includePicks`
  false) — that's what breaks the recursion. Don't conflate these.
- **Projected draft slot ranks STARTERS, never roster totals.** `originSlot`
  calls `startingStrength`; a team hoarding ranked bench bodies is not a
  contender and its future first is not a late pick. Summing whole rosters
  shipped once and priced a rebuilder's 2027 first as a 1.09.
- **There is ONE lineup filler: `fillLineup(assets, slots)` + `offenseStartingSlots(lg)`.**
  Both the value model (`startingStrength`) and the points model (`optimalOffense`)
  go through it. Never hand-roll a "top-K by value" lineup — that shipped for
  months and started two QBs in a 1QB league.
- **`startableIds(roster)` before any lineup.** Sleeper's `players` array includes
  taxi and IR. Points lineups always exclude them; the value model excludes them
  from PV (`yearsOut=0`) but includes them in FV, because taxi eligibility expires.
  `isSidelined(pid)` additionally benches Out/Doubtful/IR/PUP. Questionable starts.
- **Score projections with `projPoints(p, lg, src)`, not `p[src]`.** The baked-in
  totals use one fixed rule set (INT −1); `leagueScorePoints` rescores from the raw
  stat line so each league gets its own number.
- **Projected points rank rosters; `championshipOdds()` says who WINS.** 6 of 10
  make the playoffs and three single-week rounds decide it, so title odds are
  nowhere near linear in points. Never answer a "should I make this trade" question
  with points alone. Every modeling constant lives in the `SIM` object — tune there,
  and re-run the sensitivity sweep before trusting a flipped conclusion.
- **Trades have two sides.** `championshipOdds` takes `whatIf` keyed by roster id;
  model what the RIVAL gives up too. Buying DJ Moore off the #2 team is worth more
  than buying the same player from a bottom feeder, and a one-sided model misses it.
- **The site is `site/`**, served as static files (`python -m http.server`).
  No npm, no build step. Don't introduce one.

## Dynasty strategy skills

Roster-management doctrine lives in a skill family, not in improvisation. Load the
relevant one before answering any contend/rebuild/trade question:

| Skill | Use it for |
|---|---|
| `dynasty-championship-equity-horizon` | Scoring any multi-year plan. **Sets the horizon.** |
| `dynasty-roster-phase-diagnosis` | Which phase is this roster in: contend / retool / rebuild / dead zone |
| `dynasty-rebuild-clock` | Running or auditing a rebuild, and when to flip |
| `dynasty-age-curve-timing` | Buy/hold/sell by age. VALUE curve vs PRODUCTION curve |
| `dynasty-pick-portfolio-valuation` | Pricing picks as a probabilistic portfolio |
| `dynasty-league-format-leverage` | What THIS format's slots and playoff field imply |
| `dynasty-trade-construction` | Shaping an actual offer |
| `dynasty-replacement-level` | Pricing any bench body, backup or depth piece against what is FREE. Owns the waiver/FAAB channel and the QB-count call. |
| `dynasty-player-evaluation` | A question about ONE player, and the hard line between what the repo can measure about him and what it cannot |

**Replacement level is the baseline for every depth question.** 46% of projected
skill players are unrostered in Password is taco and a 196-point QB is free, so a
backup is only worth its gap over the pool. `dynasty-replacement-level` carries the
measurement and is the authority if another skill disagrees about how many QBs to
roster.

**Never quote a title-odds delta from one Monte Carlo run.** At 6000 sims the SE on
a 1.4% baseline is ~0.15pp, which is large enough to flip the sign of a real effect.
Pair seeds, report the spread, and refuse any delta under your own noise floor.
`node site/js/dynasty-claims.test.js` re-derives every measured number the skills
quote straight from the data files, so run it after any `build_ktc.py` or
`build_site_data.py` refresh.

**The horizon rule is not optional.** A rebuild sacrifices years 1-3 by construction,
so scoring one on a short window rejects every rebuild ever proposed. Use
`H >= max(7, years_to_flip + 4)`, state the discount, and run the discount
sensitivity before reporting a verdict. This exact error shipped once already:
a teardown was scored over 3 years, lost, and was reported as refuted.

**Two curves, never interchangeable.** `ageRetention` is dynasty VALUE (prices a
whole remaining career). `productionRetention` is season POINTS. Value leads
production by about a season, which is why the sell trigger fires while a player
is still producing.

## When you ship

- `node --check site/js/app.js` for syntax
- **`python ../.agents/scripts/verify-app.py "Fantasy Football"` before claiming any UI change works.**
  It drives all 23 mapped features headlessly (every route, both league sub-tabs, the roster
  blueprint, Cmd+K, the phone hamburger at 420px) and exits 1 on a failure or a console error.
  A new view ships with its entry in `.agents/feature-map.json`, in the same change.
- `node site/js/origin-slot.test.js && node site/js/starting-lineup.test.js && node site/js/title-odds.test.js && node site/js/projections.test.js && node site/js/team-needs.test.js && node site/js/trade-picks.test.js && node site/js/trade-consolidation.test.js && node site/js/pick-fv.test.js && node site/js/dynasty-claims.test.js && node site/js/gibbs-tiers-source.test.js && node site/js/gibbs-fullppr.test.js && node --test site/js/jacob-gibbs.test.js` to run the test suite
- **"Refresh the data" always means the whole pipeline: `python projections/build_all.py`**
  (the full run, not `--core`). It walks the dependency order — Sleeper dump, KTC, site
  data, IDP, player info, offense components, scores, environment, SOS, categories,
  context, history — and stamps `site/data/build-info.js` from real mtimes. Never ship a
  partial refresh that leaves one fresh column beside stale ones; on the phone they look
  identical. One source it can't run because it needs a hand-fed input file:
  `site/data/build_jacob_gibbs.py`. Run `site/data/build_expert_rankings.py` too if
  `_expert_sources.json` changed. Everything else is in the pipeline.
- **Season-long market lines come from BettingPros now, not a PrizePicks dump.**
  `projections/fetch_season_props.py` (in `build_all.py`, key-free, scriptable) pulls the
  season board off BettingPros' public API, which scouts ~9 books — PrizePicks, Caesars,
  DraftKings, Kalshi, BetMGM, Hard Rock, theScore, Underdog, BetRivers — and returns a
  consensus line **plus both sides' prices**, so a line can be devigged. It writes
  `season-props.json`; `build_offense_components.py` reads that and falls back to the old
  `prizepicks-nfl-season-lines.json` only if it's missing. PrizePicks is still merged in
  for breadth because it is the one board carrying **season receptions** (78 players) —
  no real book posts that market.
- **A prop's PRICE is half its information, and only the consensus pair may be devigged.**
  `projections/devig.py` turns the two-sided consensus price into the market's expected
  value, and `season-props.json` carries both (`posted_line` as boarded, `line` as the
  devigged mean, plus `fair_prob_over`). Three rules that are load-bearing:
  - **Never devig `best_over` against `best_under`.** They are the best price on each side
    from different books AT DIFFERENT LINES (97 of 107 rec-yard props disagree). Olave's
    `-140` over belongs to a 999.5 line, not the 1050.5 consensus; paired naively it reads
    as a big over lean when the real consensus pair is `-115/-110`, a 0.5pp nudge.
  - **Counts solve with Poisson, uncapped, no free parameter.** TD lines move on a half-TD
    grid, so a book that means 4.3 posts 5.5 and charges for it — 29% of rush-TD props sit
    >5pp off 50/50 vs 0% of pass-yard props. Solving `P(X>=6)=0.27` puts Kyler Murray at
    4.33 rush TDs. This is where price adds real information; yardage medians barely move.
  - **Extreme yardage leans are alt rungs and get DROPPED, not estimated.** The tell is
    clustering: 8 different players posted at exactly 749.5. Past a 10pp lean the answer
    would come entirely from the guessed CV in `devig.CV`, so the row is dropped and
    Sleeper fills the slot with a visible borrow flag instead.
- **Call `grab_prizepicks_browser.py` once per refresh, not in a loop.** DataDome escalates
  to an interstitial after a few grabs in one session (hit 2026-08-18 on the 4th). A failed
  grab leaves the previous board on disk untouched and `build_all.py` reports 15/16 rather
  than pretending, which is the intended behaviour.
- **The PrizePicks browser dump is scripted now** — `projections/grab_prizepicks_browser.py`,
  in the pipeline. It opens a real **headed** Chrome for ~15s, lets DataDome's script set its
  cookie, then fetches the JSON:API from inside the page and pipes it to `fetch_prizepicks.py`.
  **Do not "optimize" it to headless**: verified 2026-08-18 that the identical code headless
  gets a `geo.captcha-delivery.com` 403 while headed returns 200 / 1351 rows. The visible
  window IS the mechanism. `curl_cffi` with Chrome TLS impersonation still 403s, which is why
  `fetch_prizepicks.py`'s own live path stays dead.
- **The site is hosted, so a local rebuild is not done.** `Fantasy Football/site/` ships
  inside the `trevor-apps` Cloudflare Pages bundle as `ff/`. After any data refresh or UI
  change, re-stage + deploy:
  `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File ..\.agents\scripts\deploy-phone-apps.ps1 -Deploy`
- `python site/data/fetch_sleeper.py && python site/data/build_site_data.py` to refresh
  rosters + the player dump only. **Do this before answering any lineup question** —
  `injury_status` goes stale fast, and a stale dump silently starts an IR player.
- `python site/data/build_ktc.py` if KTC data may have changed
- **A new Gibbs board is two commands, and the second is not optional.** He publishes it as
  images: transcribe to `site/data/_sources/<date>.csv`, run `build_jacob_gibbs.py` on it
  (`--updated-at --source --title`) for the rank column, then
  `python site/data/_sources/build_gibbs_brief.py` for `site/gibbs-tiers.html`. Skip the
  second and the column moves while the tier board lies. `gibbs-tiers-source.test.js` pins
  the board to a second, independently typed transcription; regenerate that TSV from the CSV
  and the test stops testing anything. Full detail in `docs/SESSION_LOG.md`.
- **All three leagues are full PPR; Gibbs publishes half.** `build_gibbs_fullppr.py` derives the
  full-PPR board (run it between the two commands above) and is the third command in that chain.
  It re-sorts RB/WR/TE only, by the reception bonus only, and holds every QB slot and tier size.
  It is a DERIVED board and must never be presented as his. `gibbs-fullppr.test.js` asserts those
  promises and each of its guards was proven to fail on a corrupted board.
- `python site/data/build_expert_rankings.py` after editing `site/data/_expert_sources.json`
  (the hand-editable expert-ranking sources); regenerates `site/data/expert-rankings.js`
  with Sleeper IDs resolved. This is how you add a new analyst's rank column
  (Gibbs, Kiorkof, ...) alongside the Vegas/Sleeper context. Toggle columns on the Sources page.
- Smoke-test by booting `python -m http.server 8765` in `site/` and opening
  http://localhost:8765
- Don't `git commit` unless explicitly asked; the user controls the commit
  log.

## House style for code

- Vanilla ES, no frameworks
- Helpers defined in `site/js/app.js` (single-file)
- DOM via the `h(...)` helper at the top of app.js
- Tier-sheet aesthetic: flat-by-default, color carries meaning, no em dashes,
  no decorative gradients, no SaaS purple
- Comments: short. Explain *why* something exists when the why isn't obvious.
  Don't comment what the code already says.

## Lean Runtime

Caveman + Ponytail are active by default in this project through local skills, hooks, Cursor rules, and MCP entries. Keep communication terse, preserve exact technical details, and choose the smallest correct implementation: existing code, stdlib, native platform, installed dependency, then minimum new code. Full rule: `.agents/rules/lean-token-and-yagni.md`.
## Working Norms

Requested improvements are implementation scope. If Trevor asks to add, apply, install, wire, improve, or make something work here, make the durable project change after reading local context. Confirm only for destructive/outward-facing actions, credentials, frozen snapshots, or genuinely ambiguous targets.
